s' product ID. Then, get its variants. However, the list_all_product_types function is available. But the user might not know the product ID, so I need to use that function to find it. \n\nWait, the user mentioned \"Wireless Earbuds\" as the product name. So I can use list_all_product_types to find the product ID for that name. Once I have the product ID, get_product_details to see its variants. Then, find the item IDs that match the user's specified attributes. \n\nThis seems like a multi-step process. Let me start with the first step: finding the user ID via email.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"find_user_id_by_email\", \"arguments\": {\"email\": \"liam.moore6985@example.com\"}}\n",
